        "content": "Infrastructure statistics describe the railway available for use; traffic statistics describe activity on it. UIC distinguishes the length of lines from the length of tracks and reports passenger-kilometres and tonne-kilometres alongside other measures. A route with additional parallel tracks therefore requires a different interpretation from a newly connected destination. Likewise, the number of passenger journeys and the distance those passengers travel answer different questions. [s1]\n\nComparisons need particular care when the reporting organization or its activities change. UIC explicitly identifies corporate restructuring, subsidiaries, privatization, and differences in business scope as challenges for consistent railway statistics. An apparent national trend should therefore be checked against the coverage of the contributing railway companies before it is explained as a change in travel demand or infrastructure provision. [s1]",
        "source_ids": ["s1"]
      },
      {
        "id": "passenger-services-and-experience",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "Passenger services are more specific than a line on a map",
        "content": "Passenger experience depends on the particular train and service offered. Fadak’s official website, for example, describes compartment accommodation, sleeping facilities, entertainment, and catering. These descriptions establish what this operator advertises; they are not independent measurements of comfort, punctuality, or customer satisfaction. They also should not be generalized to every Iranian passenger train. The undated website was inspected after this page’s research cutoff, so its exact offerings on the cutoff date remain unconfirmed. [s3]\n\nA useful account of rail transport consequently needs both physical and operational evidence. A railway map can explain connections, while dated service information establishes which passenger journeys are actually offered. Performance data are needed for conclusions about reliability or effectiveness. This page currently provides the conceptual distinctions and historical foundation; a complete contemporary synthesis still requires verified operating and traffic evidence.",
        "source_ids": ["s3"]
      }
    ],
